title: ActThreeNotes
act: Mine
location: Mine
scenario: The collapse
style: note
---
Act III, one shift in the mine, a separate root scene with its levels as child scenes (the gallery, the flooded gallery, the deep level). The lamp holds three measures of oil, and each descent burns one. Three ways down from the gallery to the deep level, each opened or not by Act I (the rope from the wheel, Nan's remedy against the cold water, or the long way, which burns one more measure). Jory, the carvings of the true border, the steward trapped in the gallery, the tally and the echo (a project of its own). The act ends at the camp when Jory is found or lost, or when the oil is out. #line:ActThreeNotes_0100
===

title: Events
act: Mine
location: Mine
scenario: The collapse
quest: jory
when: once
when: $act == Act.Mine
when: here() == "Mine"
---
The mine camp, under the hill. Tents, a fire, and miners who don't look up. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Camp_0100
Gudrun: Foreman Gudrun. You came. Good. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Camp_0200_Gudrun
Gudrun: Jory went into the old gallery before it fell. The lift goes down that far. Past the rubble there are three ways to the deep level. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Camp_0300_Gudrun
Gudrun: The old shaft, if you have a rope. The flooded gallery, if the cold doesn't stop your heart. Or the long way round, which eats lamp oil. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Camp_0400_Gudrun
Gudrun: Three measures of oil in your lamp. Every trip down the lift burns one. Make them count. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Camp_0500_Gudrun
<<set $quest_jory to QuestState.Active>>
<<quest_changed jory>>
<<if $quest_page == QuestState.Succeeded>>
    You think of the charter's page. "As the carvings show." The carvings must be down there. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Camp_0600
<<else>>
    Gudrun: And the lantern folk are down there. Carvings on the wall, that glow green. Old miners' nonsense, or not. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Camp_0700_Gudrun
<<endif>>
<<set $quest_carvings to QuestState.Active>>
<<quest_changed carvings>>
<<if $corvin_in_mine>>
    Gudrun: Your steward came at first light. Went down the lift without a word to me. He hasn't come up. #line:Events.3344e1f8_Camp_0800_Gudrun
    <<set $quest_corvin to QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed corvin>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Events
act: Mine
location: Anywhere
scenario: The lights
quest: echo
when: $echo_answered and $quest_echo != QuestState.Succeeded
---
// The echo is a project of its own, but it shares the game's variables: the story sees what it set.
Somewhere far below, the echo has fallen silent. The miners will talk about it for a year. #line:Events.76b09685_0100
<<set $quest_echo to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed echo>>
===

title: Events
act: Mine
location: Mine
scenario: The collapse
when: once
when: $act == Act.Mine
when: here() == "Mine" and $quest_jory != QuestState.NotStarted
when: $quest_jory != QuestState.Active or $oil <= 0
---
// The end of the third act, at the camp: Jory found, or lost with the last of the oil.
<<if $jory_found>>
    The lift comes up into grey dawn light, with Jory leaning on your shoulder. The camp cheers. #line:Events.8dd08405_0100
    Gudrun: You brought him back. I won't forget it. Nobody under this hill will. #line:Events.8dd08405_0200_Gudrun
<<else>>
    <<if $quest_jory == QuestState.Active>>
        <<set $quest_jory to QuestState.Failed>>
        <<quest_changed jory>>
    <<endif>>
    Gudrun: The oil's out. We dig for him from this side, and we pray. #mood:sad #line:Events.8dd08405_0300_Gudrun
<<endif>>
<<if $quest_carvings == QuestState.Active>>
    <<set $quest_carvings to QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed carvings>>
<<endif>>
<<if $quest_corvin == QuestState.Active>>
    The steward climbs out of the lift at the last moment, grey with dust, and walks off without a word. #line:Events.8dd08405_0400
    <<set $quest_corvin to QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed corvin>>
<<endif>>
<<if $quest_tally == QuestState.Active or $quest_tally == QuestState.Offered>>
    <<set $quest_tally to QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed tally>>
<<endif>>
<<if $quest_echo == QuestState.Offered>>
    <<set $quest_echo to QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed echo>>
<<endif>>
Two days later, the valley goes down to Ashcombe for the spring fair, and the hearing. #line:Events.8dd08405_0500
<<set $act to Act.Fair>>
<<set $fair_up to true>>
<<set $pell_in_village to true>>
<<set $corvin_in_mine to false>>
<<set $corvin_at_fair to $corvin_fate != CorvinFate.Left>>
<<end_day>>
<<end_day>>
<<go VillageRoad>>
===

title: Gudrun
act: Mine
location: Mine
scenario: The collapse
quest: tally
when: $act == Act.Mine
when: $quest_tally == QuestState.NotStarted
---
Gudrun: One more thing, map maker. The tally board. Every miner hangs a token when they go down and takes it back when they come up. #line:Gudrun.262ffdd1_0100_Gudrun
Gudrun: My eyes are tired. Count them for me when you can. I need to know who is still under the hill. #line:Gudrun.262ffdd1_0200_Gudrun
<<set $quest_tally to QuestState.Active>>
<<quest_changed tally>>
Gudrun: And if you hear a voice asking riddles down there, that's the echo of the deep level. Answer it, and it goes quiet. Nobody has. #line:Gudrun.262ffdd1_0300_Gudrun
<<set $quest_echo to QuestState.Offered>>
<<quest_changed echo>>
===

title: Gudrun
act: All
location: Mine
scenario: The collapse
when: always
---
=> Gudrun: Lamp oil is life down there. Don't waste it on sightseeing. #line:Gudrun.c3a63ab1_0100_Gudrun
=> Gudrun: [plural value={$oil} one="One measure" other="% measures" /] left in your lamp. <<if $oil > 0>> #line:Gudrun.c3a63ab1_0200_Gudrun
=> Gudrun: Your lamp is dry. Nobody goes down without light. <<if $oil <= 0>> #line:Gudrun.c3a63ab1_0300_Gudrun
=> Gudrun: You answered the echo? Nobody answers the echo. <<if $echo_answered>> #line:Gudrun.c3a63ab1_0400_Gudrun
=> Gudrun: Thank you for the count. <<if $quest_tally == QuestState.Succeeded>> #line:Gudrun.c3a63ab1_0500_Gudrun
===

title: TallyBoard
act: Mine
location: Mine
scenario: The collapse
quest: tally
when: $quest_tally == QuestState.Active
---
<<if $jory_found>>
    <<set $tally to 12>>
<<else>>
    <<set $tally to 11>>
<<endif>>
You count the tokens on the pegs. [plural value={$tally} one="One miner" other="% miners" /] came up. #line:TallyBoard.cd7a6395_0100
<<if $jory_found>>
    Jory's token hangs on the last peg, the [ordinal value=12 one="%st" two="%nd" few="%rd" other="%th" /]. Everyone is out. #line:TallyBoard.cd7a6395_0200
<<else>>
    One peg is empty, the [ordinal value=12 one="%st" two="%nd" few="%rd" other="%th" /]. Jory's. #line:TallyBoard.cd7a6395_0300
<<endif>>
<<set $quest_tally to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed tally>>
===

title: TallyBoard
act: All
location: Mine
scenario: The collapse
when: always
---
The tally board. Twelve pegs, twelve names chalked above them. #line:TallyBoard.67bc372d_0100
===

title: LiftDown
act: Mine
location: Mine
scenario: The collapse
when: $act == Act.Mine
---
// Each trip down the lift burns a measure of the lamp's oil.
<<if $oil <= 0>>
    Gudrun: Your lamp is dry. I won't send you down without light. #line:LiftDown.92d21ea7_0100_Gudrun
<<else>>
    <<set $oil to $oil - 1>>
    The lift creaks down into the dark. Your lamp burns lower. [plural value={$oil} one="One measure" other="% measures" /] left. #line:LiftDown.92d21ea7_0200
    <<go Lift>>
<<endif>>
===

title: MineToVillage
act: Mine
location: Mine
scenario: The collapse
when: $act == Act.Mine
---
Gudrun: Not while Jory is under the hill. Nobody leaves the camp. #line:MineToVillage.de5fdb53_0100_Gudrun
===
